Problem Description:
Implement a D latch using an always block.

module top_module (
	input d,
	input ena,
	output logic q
);

Erroneous Implementation:

always_ff @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
	if (reset)
		q <= 1'b0;
	else if (ena)
		q <= d;
end

endmodule

Feedback:
m2014_q4a.sv:129: error: Unable to bind wire/reg/memory `reset' in `tb.top_module1'
m2014_q4a.sv:129: error: Unable to elaborate condition expression.
2 error(s) during elaboration.

```verilog
module top_module (
	input d,
	input ena,
	output logic q
);

// A D latch is level-sensitive, not edge-triggered.
// In SystemVerilog, 'always_latch' is used to explicitly describe latch logic.
// When 'ena' is high, the output 'q' follows the input 'd'.
// When 'ena' is low, 'q' retains its previous value.
always_latch begin
	if (ena)
		q <= d;
end

endmodule
```
